@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-use-sequential-task-identifiers
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use sequential task identifiers"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Task titles can change, so they cannot provide a stable reference for a task. Task identifiers must
+also comply with the domain rule that disallows clocks and randomness.
+
+## Decision
+
+Each in-memory list assigns IDs sequentially as `task-1`, `task-2`, and so on. IDs are never changed
+or reused by that list, including after a task is removed. Lookups that accept a title or ID resolve
+an ID first.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Task references survive renames and callers can use deterministic IDs in tests. IDs are unique only
+within an individual in-memory list, matching the list's storage scope.
